function show_help {
	cat <<EOF
me — sync all or part of the me.sh configuration

Usage:
  me                          List available units
  me --help                   Show this help
  me --force <any sync>       Move conflicting destinations aside, then deploy
  me all                      Sync macOS configs first, then app configs
  me bootstrap               Run every fresh-machine step in filename order
  me bootstrap <name>...     Run selected bootstrap steps, in argument order
  me app | apps               Sync all app configs
  me macos | sys | system     Sync all macOS configs
  me [app|macos] <name>...    Sync only the named configs
  me <name>...                Resolve names across configs and bootstrap
  me add <file> [--link symlink|copy] [--app name] [--dest \$HOME/...]
                              Adopt a file into a config unit and deploy it;
                              missing flags are prompted for interactively
  me remove [--delete|--unlink] <unit|file>...
                              Remove claimed files from the repo and this
                              machine; prompts for how to retire each copy
  me install                  Copy a 'me' shim into ~/bin (bakes this repo's path)
  me doctor                   Validate manifests and destination claims
  me plan [scope] [<name>...] Show config actions without deploying
  me status [app|macos] [<name>|<path>...]
                              List drifted files compactly, no diffs shown
  me diff [app|macos] [<name>|<path>...]
                              Show one combined drift diff
  me up [app|macos] [<name>|<path>...]
                              Review drift hunk by hunk, route each to base or a local fragment

A manifest unit is named by its directory (e.g. 'yojam' or 'karabiner'). A
legacy name matches either its config directory or its configure script. With
no scope, names are looked up in app and macOS configs plus bootstrap units;
collisions require an explicit scope. Bootstrap membership and order come from
bootstrap/NN-name.sh.

Examples:
  me add ~/.gitconfig         Adopt a file: prompts for link type, unit, dest
  me add ~/.vimrc --link symlink --app vim
                              Non-interactive adoption into an existing unit
  me add ~/notes.conf --app mytool --scope apps --copy --dest '\$HOME/.config/mytool/notes.conf'
                              Create a new unit with a static copy
  me remove git               Remove every file the 'git' unit claims from the
                              repo and delete its deployed symlinks/copies
  me remove ~/.gitconfig      Find which row claims that path and undo it
  me remove configs/apps/git/gitconfig
                              Same, matched by repository source path
  me remove ghostty --unlink  Retire deployed symlinks but keep their content
                              in place as plain files
  me app karabiner            Sync one app config
  me karabiner                Same: unambiguous, found in app configs
  me bin                      Same: 'me system bin'
  me bootstrap               Prepare a fresh Mac
  me bootstrap homebrew-install
                              Re-run just Homebrew acquisition
  me homebrew                Reconcile installed packages with the Brewfile
  me app git ghostty          Several configs in one run
  me diff                     Check every config for drift in one combined diff
  me diff agents              Preview machine-local drift in agent configs
  me status                   List every drifted file without showing diffs
  me status app               Same, restricted to app configs
  me diff ~/.gitconfig        Scope a diff by deployed path
  me diff ghostty/config      Path filters match either side on '/' boundaries
  me up                       Review drift everywhere, route hunks to base or local fragments
  me doctor                   Validate the complete config registry
  me plan yojam               Validate and preview one unit
  me plan app                 Preview every app unit

Deployment refuses destinations it does not already own: a symlink row whose
destination is a regular file or directory, a copy row blocked by a directory,
or a managed file blocked by a directory. One such conflict fails the whole unit
before anything is written. '--force' (or '-f', accepted anywhere in the
argument list) moves each conflicting destination to
'<dest>.me-backup-<timestamp>' and continues. 'me plan --force' shows those
backups as 'backup' lines.

Config failures never stop the run; they are summarized at the end and reported
with a non-zero exit code. Bootstrap is an ordered dependency chain and stops
at the first failure.

Managed files declare themselves with a sibling '<file>.d/' overlay directory
containing a 'dest' marker; they deploy as a base-plus-overlays composition.
Manifest 'copies' rows are direct materialized copies without overlays. Local
changes to either kind stay in the deployed copy. 'me status' lists that drift
compactly; 'me diff' shows it; 'me up' reviews it hunk by hunk and pulls what
you approve back into the repo source. All three accept an optional scope plus
names and/or path filters, covering every config when none are given. A path
filter matches on '/' boundaries against either side — the repo source or the
deployed destination — so 'ghostty/config', '~/.gitconfig', and 'configs/apps/git'
all work; arguments containing '/' are always paths, bare words resolve as
config names first, and multiple filters union.

'me remove' undoes 'me add': it deletes manifest rows (and their copied repo
sources) plus the deployed destinations. Bare-word arguments are manifest unit
names and remove every row they own; arguments containing '/' match by deployed
path or repo source. Deployed symlinks are deleted by default or replaced with
a plain file holding their content via --unlink; live copies of static-copy
rows are kept unless you confirm deletion (--delete skips all prompts). Units
left owning nothing after removal, including their config.yml, are pruned.
Managed (<base>.d) files are out of scope.

Requires yq for manifests and YAML/TOML fragments.

Config directories may replace their configure scripts with config.yml. Its
'symlinks' and 'copies' rows are deployed safely, sibling managed files are
auto-discovered, and an executable post.sh runs last. Static copies and managed
files participate in 'me diff' and 'me up'. Use 'me plan' to preview deployment.

Shell completion (zsh) lives in lib/completion/_me and is installed into
~/.zsh/completions by the shell config.
EOF
}

# --- Main ------------------------------------------------------------------

# --force is global: strip it wherever it appears so subcommand parsing is
# unaffected. Only deployment reads it.
declare -a passthrough_args=()
for arg in "$@"; do
	case "$arg" in
		-f|--force) ME_FORCE=1 ;;
		*) passthrough_args+=("$arg") ;;
	esac
done
set -- ${passthrough_args[@]+"${passthrough_args[@]}"}

if (( $# == 0 )); then
	show_list
	exit 0
fi

case "$1" in
	-h|--help)
		show_help
		exit 0
		;;
	-l|--list)
		show_list
		exit 0
		;;
	--completion-names)
		# Internal: consumed by lib/completion/_me.
		show_completion_names
		exit 0
		;;
	add)
		shift
		run_add "$@"
		finish
		;;
	remove|rm)
		shift
		run_remove "$@"
		finish
		;;
	install)
		if (( $# > 1 )); then
			error "'install' takes no additional arguments"
			exit 1
		fi
		install_me_shim
		;;
	doctor)
		if (( $# > 1 )); then
			error "'doctor' takes no additional arguments"
			exit 1
		fi
		run_doctor
		exit $?
		;;
	plan)
		shift
		scope=""
		if (( $# > 0 )); then
			case "$1" in
				all) scope=all; shift ;;
				app|apps) scope="$APPS_SCOPE"; shift ;;
				mac|macos|sys|system) scope="$MACOS_SCOPE"; shift ;;
			esac
		fi
		if [[ "$scope" == all && $# -gt 0 ]]; then
			error "'me plan all' takes no config names"
			exit 1
		elif (( $# > 0 )); then
			resolve_args "${scope:-$CONFIG_SCOPE}" "$@"
		elif [[ "$scope" == "$APPS_SCOPE" || "$scope" == "$MACOS_SCOPE" ]]; then
			select_units_in_scope "$scope"
		else
			select_all_config_units
		fi
		run_plan_selected
		finish
		;;
	bootstrap)
		shift
		if (( $# == 0 )); then
			select_bootstrap_scripts
		else
			resolve_args "$BOOTSTRAP_SCOPE" "$@"
		fi
		run_bootstrap_selected
		finish
		;;
	all)
		if (( $# > 1 )); then
			error "'all' takes no additional arguments"
			exit 1
		fi
		message "Syncing everything..."
		run_scope "$MACOS_SCOPE"
		run_scope "$APPS_SCOPE"
		finish
		;;
	status)
		shift
		parse_drift_args "$@"
		run_status
		finish
		;;
	diff)
		shift
		parse_drift_args "$@"
		run_drift show
		finish
		;;
	up|absorb)
		shift
		parse_drift_args "$@"
		run_drift absorb
		finish
		;;
	app|apps)
		shift
		if (( $# == 0 )); then
			message "Syncing all app configs..."
			run_scope "$APPS_SCOPE"
			finish
		fi
		resolve_args "$APPS_SCOPE" "$@"
		run_selected
		finish
		;;
	mac|macos|sys|system)
		shift
		if (( $# == 0 )); then
			message "Syncing all macOS configs..."
			run_scope "$MACOS_SCOPE"
			finish
		fi
		resolve_args "$MACOS_SCOPE" "$@"
		run_selected
		finish
		;;
	*)
		resolve_args "$ANY_SCOPE" "$@"
		run_selected
		finish
		;;
esac
